From 239500595b7fbf3b72e39f597c36b56766f3be0c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Onni Hakala <onni@flaky.build>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 20:37:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Reuse type check results of dependents when signatures
 are unchanged

When a module is recompiled but its ExCk chunk (exports, signatures,
deprecations) is identical, runtime dependents without previous warnings
reuse their type check result. Behaviour checks and @after_verify
callbacks still run, as they may call into the recompiled module.

Phoenix app with 160 routes: editing a LiveView no longer type checks the
router again, hot reload 130ms -> 84ms.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LvES9Ck5Yzq161ZVv9orsy
